# Project Agents Context
# Last updated: 2026-09-27

## Project identity
- **CyberVault** — password manager with split-trust architecture: browser extension (MV3 service worker + popup), Core API (`src/infrastructure/api`, port 3010), Plus entitlement/challenge service (`plus/`, port 3011).
- Stack: TypeScript (strict), WebCrypto (PBKDF2 600k / HKDF), Jest + ts-jest, esbuild bundling (`scripts/build-extension.mjs`), optional SonarQube.

## Architecture
- `src/background/auditor.ts` — service worker: message router, all handlers, release/step-up/managed-release logic. Sole entry point for extension messaging.
- `src/background/message-types.ts` — the message contract; re-exported by `auditor.ts`. Content scripts and popup import from it so they cannot drift.
- `src/background/credential-release.ts` — release path (binding proof → guard → key derivation → decrypt). Fails closed on every failure path.
- `src/domain/services/autofill/` — origin canonicalization, opaque index, authoring, step-up binding rules, autofill guard.
- `src/infrastructure/crypto/master-key-manager.ts` — vault init/unlock, session key (`cybervault_session_key`, 15-min `SESSION_DURATION_MS`).
- `src/ui/popup/popup.ts|html` — popup UI; sends typed messages only.
- `src/ui/content-scripts/` — `autocomplete.js` (form fill), `managed-decrypt.js`, `inject.js`.
- Storage: `chrome.storage.session` holds `cybervault_vek` + `cybervault_session_key` + `cybervault_unlock_state`; `chrome.storage.local` holds `cybervault_cred_records` + `cybervault_cred_index` (ciphertext only).

## Current state
- Stage: **WU-3 (CRITICAL-3) implementation complete, awaiting orchestrator verification and commit.** Branch `fix/pentest-script-rdd`. Nothing committed by the agent.

## Objectives
1. ✅ WU-1 / WU-2 (prior sessions) — origin authority, managed-release contract fixes.
2. ✅ WU-3 — extension-side credential release path wired end to end (VEK persistence, authoring writer, step-up senders, popup senders, behavioural tests).
3. ⏳ Orchestrator verification + commit (explicitly out of agent scope).

## Project conventions
- English for all code, comments, tests, docs; no AI attribution in commits; conventional commits only.
- No new dependencies. Do not touch `plus/`, `plus/admin/`, Docker.
- Never weaken: ExactMatch guard, step-up binding re-check, JTI consumption. `origin.ts` is the sole origin authority.
- Regex-on-source assertions in tests constrain refactors — read them before editing `auditor.ts`.

## External dependencies
- Node 18+ (global `fetch`, WebCrypto). Playwright e2e requires Chrome (not installed here). SonarQube scanner CLI not installed.

## Points of attention
- **tsc baseline = 809 errors** (pre-existing, mostly `plus/admin` JSX). Any edit must keep it at 809.
- **jest baseline = 908 passed / 921 total** (52 of 53 suites, 13 skipped) after WU-3.
- Never write `password`/`totpSecret` inside a `chrome.storage.local.set(...)` body in `auditor.ts` — `tests/extension/sw-contract.test.ts` uses a non-greedy regex that can overrun to the next `)`.
- 15-min (`master-key-manager`) vs 30-min (`SESSION_WINDOW_MS`) session window discrepancy is reported, not silently unified.
- `.agents` and `.progress` are gitignored runtime state, not deliverables.
